<title>BELGIUM: Farm Council to discuss veterinary mandate again on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Farm Council to discuss veterinary mandate again on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler on Monday briefed farm ministers on the state of negotiations with the United States and other major trading partners on the mutual recognition of veterinary standards.</p>
<p>A Commission spokesman said ministers will return to the issue on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The European Commission is seeking instructions before starting a further round of talks in Washington on March 24 in a bid to reach agreement before the March 31 deadline.</p>
<p>&quot;They are at a delicate stage,&quot; the spokesman said, noting that Fischler's briefing was given in restricted session.</p>
<p>The spokesman declined to give further details.</p>
<p>Important problems remain and if no agreement is reached by the end of the month, imports of all U.S. beef, poultry and other animal and plant products would be subject to strict controls.</p>
</text>
